          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            induces a smash product on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %p
            This is the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            which are symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
            (such as the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/highly+structured+spectra"} highly structured spectra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-modules"} S-modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+functors"} excisive functors
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal category of spectra
            for more on this. Passing to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            under the smash product. Under mild assumptions, this is the essentially unique symmetric tensor product with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            (
            %a{:href => "#Shipley01"}> Shipley 01
            ).
          %h3#history History
          %p
            Historically the discussion proceeded in the opposite direction: available variants of the construction of smash products on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            (the “handicrafted” or “naive” smash products
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Boardman65"} Boardman 65
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Adams74"} Adams 74, part III, section 4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            structure
            %em only
            after passage to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/highly+structured+spectra"} highly structured spectra
            were discovered which do admit a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            in the sense of 1-category theory, as do
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+functors"} excisive functors
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+excisive+functors"} model structure on excisive functors
          %h3#as_day_convolution_spectra As Day convolution spectra
          %p
            Many versions of the smash product of spectra,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric or not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            products on a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            version of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of “index spaces”.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            on, in particular,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            is the Day convolution product for
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            on monoidal categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+groups"} symmetric groups
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+groups"} orthogonal groups
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MMSS00"} MMSS 00, theorem 1.7 and section 21.
          %p
            Similarly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
            is Day convolution for
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            on the plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of finite pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lydakis98"}> Lydakis 98
            ).
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+with+smash+products"} functor with smash products
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#GradedCommutativity Graded commutativity
          %p
            The smash product of spectra exhibits a certain graded commutativity akin to the graded commutativity in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            (in fact, under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
            the latter maps to the former).
          %p
            This comes down to the following basic fact about the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
          #GradedCommutativityOfSmashOfSpheres.num_prop
